The '''Delgaldon Plains'''<ref name="Dooku: Jedi Lost script">[[Dooku: Jedi Lost (script)|''Dooku: Jedi Lost'' script]]</ref> were an area of plains on the [[Outer Rim Territories]] [[planet]] [[Serenno]]. When arriving on Serenno to assist the [[Serennian]] people with [[Abyssin]] [[Mercenary|mercenaries]] who had taken over the planet and the [[Carannia|capital city]], [[Jedi Master]]s [[Dooku]], [[Sifo-Dyas]], [[Lene Kostana]], and the [[protocol droid]] [[D-4]] crashed onto the Delgaldon Plains in the ''[[Truthseeker]]''. The crash landing led to D-4 being destroyed. After the crash landing, [[Jenza]] and [[Eson]] traveled to the crash site in a [[speeder]] and met up with the survivors, who together travelled to the [[Serenno Camp]].<ref name="Dooku: Jedi Lost" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Delgaldon Plains appears in the [[canon]] audiobook ''[[Dooku: Jedi Lost]]'' written by [[Cavan Scott]]<ref name="Dooku: Jedi Lost" /> and released on [[April 30]], [[2019]].<ref name="Penguin-Download">{{PenguinRandomHouse|url=books/607498/dooku-jedi-lost-star-wars-by-cavan-scott/9780593102817|text=Dooku: Jedi Lost (Star Wars)}}</ref>

